Planex antipattern_perception — why Perception is necessary
==============================================================
Shows: render function cannot express multiple denotations

[anti-pattern 1] Multiple denotations of same state
  React: 1 render fn — must branch on mode OR maintain parallel trees
  Planex: 4 independent Perception functions, same Estimate
  Registered 4 perceptions for same Estimate
  PASS — multiple denotations coexist as first-class

[anti-pattern 2] Pure-function rendering (testable)
  React: render uses hooks, needs react-test-renderer to test
  Planex: Perception is pure fn, callable directly in test
  Direct call results:
    visual: Count: 42
    a11y:   Counter value is 42
    json:   {"count": 42, "confidence": 1.00}
    log:    [LOG] count=42
  PASS — each perception is a pure function, no test renderer

[anti-pattern 3] Independent lifecycle of each denotation
  React: parallel trees are coupled to render fn, hard to remove
  Planex: each Perception is independent, can be removed at runtime
  After freeing a11y perception: count=3 (was 4)
  After invoke_all: visual=2, a11y=1 (unchanged), json=2, log=2
  PASS — independent lifecycle, removing one doesn't affect others

[anti-pattern 4] Selective invocation
  React: state change re-runs entire render, no selective update
  Planex: invoke_for_estimate runs only matching perceptions
  px_perceptions_for_estimate(count) returned 3 (expected 3)
  px_perceptions_for_estimate(other_est) returned 1 (expected 1)
  PASS — selective invocation works via Relation-like dependency tracking

=== Summary ===
Mainstream render (React/SwiftUI) requires FOUR patches:
  1. Mode branching or parallel trees for multiple denotations
  2. react-test-renderer for testing render output
  3. Conditional code throughout for independent lifecycle
  4. Re-render entire tree on state change (no selective update)

Planex Perception subsumes all four as first-class:
  1. Multiple Perception functions, same Estimate
  2. Pure function, callable directly in unit test
  3. Each Perception independent, removable at runtime
  4. invoke_for_estimate runs only matching perceptions

Perception is NECESSARY: render + patches is a strict subset.

=== Perception anti-pattern test complete ===
